{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Qpz7qCHvTdUMGmeRs5d4Wv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils derives formal specifications from C source code of GNU utilities and generates Go implementations via AI, verified by differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture:** `cmd/` per-utility binaries, `pkg/testutils/` differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` cross-platform syscall wrappers, `pkg/format/` shared formatting, `docs/` human-authored specifications, `magefiles/` build automation (excluded from generation).\n\n**Implementation state (from source_code):**\n- **Done:** pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/cat, cmd/wc, cmd/version — all have production code and tests on the working branch\n- **Missing:** cmd/sponge (rel01.2, spec complete, no code), cmd/du (rel01.3, spec complete, no code)\n\n**Current release:** rel01.2 — sponge is the next utility to implement.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nReleases 00.0 through 01.1 are effectively complete (all generation-targetable code exists in source_code). The earliest incomplete release in scope is **rel01.2 (sponge)**. Per P2, implementation and tests must be split — this session proposes the implementation task; the test task follows in a future session.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/sponge stdin buffering and file write -- sponge PRD R1, R2, R3, R4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (glob for prd*-sponge.yaml -- the sponge PRD; read it fully before writing any code)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.2-uc001-sponge.yaml (sponge use case)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.2.yaml (sponge test suite specification -- understand expected behaviors)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (reference cmd/ implementation pattern -- run() function, flag parsing, error formatting)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (second reference cmd/ implementation pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct -- understand the differential test contract your code will be tested against)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sponge/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"sponge command implementation -- reads all stdin then writes to named file\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement core sponge behavior per the sponge PRD R1 requirements: read all of standard input into a buffer before writing any output to the named file. The key invariant is that the target file must not be modified until stdin is fully consumed, enabling pipelines like 'sort file | sponge file'. When no file argument is provided, write buffered stdin to stdout.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement the -a (append) flag per the sponge PRD R2 requirements: when -a is specified, append the buffered stdin content to the existing file rather than overwriting it. Without -a, the target file is overwritten.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement safe file write per the sponge PRD requirements: use a temporary file in the same directory as the target and rename it into place to prevent partial writes from corrupting the target. Follow whatever specific write strategy the PRD specifies.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement error handling and exit codes per the sponge PRD error requirements: exit 0 on success, exit 1 on any error. Write error messages to stderr in the format 'sponge: <description>' matching the pattern used by cmd/cat (see printFileError in cmd/cat/main.go).\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the established cmd/ entry point pattern: func main() { os.Exit(run(os.Args[1:])) } with run() accepting args and returning an int exit code. See cmd/cat/main.go line 21-22 and cmd/wc/main.go line 21-22.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use flag.NewFlagSet(\\\"sponge\\\", flag.ContinueOnError) with fs.SetOutput(os.Stderr) for flag parsing, matching cmd/cat/main.go line 56-57 and cmd/wc/main.go line 38-39.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Include the copyright header and SPDX identifier matching existing cmd/ packages: '// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.' and '// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT'. Add a package doc comment with Implements: tracing back to the sponge PRD requirement IDs.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/sponge/main.go exists and compiles successfully with 'go build ./cmd/sponge/'.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"The sponge binary reads all of stdin completely before writing any output to the target file -- verified by the implementation buffering stdin fully before opening the target for write.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"The -a flag causes the binary to append buffered content to the target file rather than overwrite it.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Error messages are written to stderr in the format 'sponge: <error description>' and the binary exits 1 on any I/O failure, 0 on success.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67090,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67090},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d33e4ee-1a9b-4189-bef7-0f73296713ed","uuid":"8a7531ca-34f4-48e6-a5dd-170ed12118f8"}
